{
  "result": "Morning glow leans through the curtains like hope that never forgets to whisper about the recent storm, and the puddles lingering around the garden pots. I am trying to hold a memory of a conversation with a stranger on the train. He said the sky was a vast page waiting for our scribbles. I liked the idea because it gave permission to be accidental and brave. Since then I have been collecting small stories like river stones, some smooth and round, others sharp enough to cut a silence. A neighbor donated seeds yesterday, and the packets were full of comets and haikus. It is possible to plant new rhythms if you listen carefully. I am tired of listening only to the loud speakers claiming to explain everything. They use terms like certainty and flush all morning with advertisements. Instead I want the slower wind that knocks on the window and stays just long enough to remind me how to breathe. There is also a box of letters in the drawer marked for different horizons, and I keep promising myself that one day I will write the long one about the city that smelled like salt and cardamom. Until then I will collect the quieter vocabulary of the earth and carry light in my pockets. Today I even managed to remember the names of three constellations, and that feels like a gift. Soon the sky will be an idea again, and I will write about the ways we make friends everywhere.",
